# Workspace-level ignores for med_ocr_swiggy_mcp.
#
# rx-ocr-expo/ is its own git repo with its own .gitignore, and the backend has one too.
# This file exists because the WORKSPACE is the thing Dokploy deploys from, and a fresh
# `git init` here would otherwise sweep up credentials that the nested ignores never see.
#
# The three that actually matter, in order of how badly they would hurt:
#   backend/.env          GROQ_API_KEY and ENCRYPTION_KEY
#   backend/data/         every user's AES-encrypted Swiggy tokens + the OAuth registration
#   backend/.user-token   a working bearer token
# ENCRYPTION_KEY is the worst of them: it decrypts the tokens in data/ AND signs the OAuth
# state, so leaking both files together hands over live grocery-account sessions.

# ---- dependencies and build output ----
node_modules/
dist/
web-build/
.expo/
.metro-health-check*
*.tsbuildinfo

# Generated by rx-ocr-expo/app/tools/copy-ort-wasm.js on every install (12 MB).
rx-ocr-expo/app/public/ort/

# Expo prebuild output; regenerated from app.config.js, never edited by hand.
rx-ocr-expo/app/ios/
rx-ocr-expo/app/android/

# ---- secrets and local state ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision

# Backend runtime state. data/ holds encrypted Swiggy tokens; it belongs in a Docker volume
# on the server, never in a repo.
swiggy_instamart_mcp/instamart_app/backend/data/
swiggy_instamart_mcp/instamart_app/backend/.user-token
swiggy_instamart_mcp/instamart_app/backend/.address-id
swiggy_instamart_mcp/instamart_app/backend/server.log
swiggy_instamart_mcp/instamart_app/backend/shapes.json

# ---- logs and scratch ----
*.log
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*
*.apk

# ---- OS noise ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# NOT ignored, deliberately:
#   catalog.json        both halves ship the identical file; it is an input, not an artefact
#   .bulk-raw/          the per-term search dumps catalog.json was built from
#   Dockerfile, docker-compose.yml, DEPLOY.md   needed by Dokploy to build
#   .env.example        the template; it carries no values
